16:T47a,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":"Understanding Daily Namaz Timings: How Prayer Times Are Calculated, Waqt Boundaries, and Sunnah Guidelines","description":"How namaz timings are calculated scientifically: Asr shadow rules (Hanafi vs Shafi'i), Fajr twilight angles, and prohibited prayer times explained.","image":["https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1542810634-71277d95dcbb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80"],"datePublished":"2026-10-14T09:30:00Z","dateModified":"2026-10-14T09:30:00Z","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Dr. Ziyad Al-Farabi (Astronomer & Islamic Scholar)","url":"https://namaz-e-shariq.com/about"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Namaz-e-Shariq","url":"https://namaz-e-shariq.com","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://namaz-e-shariq.com/web-app-manifest-512x512.png"}},"mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://namaz-e-shariq.com/blog/understanding-namaz-timings-calculation-methods"},"keywords":"asr namaz time, asr prayer time, fajr namaz time, maghrib namaz time, maghrib prayer time, isha namaz time, isha prayer time, today maghrib namaz time, prayer calculation"}17:T76d,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Why do Hanafi and Shafi’i Asr prayer times differ?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The juristic disagreement centers on the shadow length requirement. In the Shafi’i, Maliki, and Hanbali schools, Asr starts when an object’s shadow equals its own length plus its midday shadow (Factor 1). In the Hanafi school, Asr starts when the shadow reaches twice the object’s length plus midday shadow (Factor 2), typically 45 to 60 minutes later."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the three strictly prohibited prayer times?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The three times when any prayer (including Nafl and Janazah) is strictly disliked (Makruh Tahrimi) are: 1) From sunrise until the sun has risen about a spear’s length (15-20 minutes after sunrise); 2) Exactly at solar zenith (Zawal) until the sun passes its peak (5 minutes before Dhuhr); 3) When the sun turns pale yellow until it completely sinks below the horizon."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is true dawn (Fajr Sadiq) versus false dawn (Fajr Kadhib)?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"False dawn is a vertical pillar of faint light that appears in the eastern sky, followed by temporary darkness. True dawn is a horizontal band of white light that spreads along the eastern horizon, signaling the start of Fajr and the time to begin fasting."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does altitude or elevation above sea level affect prayer times?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Elevation raises the observer above the geometric horizon, causing the sun to appear to rise earlier and set later. For every 1,000 meters of elevation, sunrise occurs roughly 1.5 minutes earlier and sunset occurs roughly 1.5 minutes later, requiring an elevation depression correction in high mountain cities."}}]}c:["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-950 min-h-screen py-10 transition-colors duration-200","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$16"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://namaz-e-shariq.com\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Articles\",\"item\":\"https://namaz-e-shariq.com/blog\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"Understanding Daily Namaz Timings: How Prayer Times Are Calculated, Waqt Boundaries, and Sunnah Guidelines\",\"item\":\"https://namaz-e-shariq.com/blog/understanding-namaz-timings-calculation-methods\"}]}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$17"}}],"$L18"]}]
